MediVault-EC2-Role
        |
        └── S3 permissions
             |
             └── medivault-scan-images-bucket01

Step - 1: Create the IAM role
AWS Console → IAM → Roles → Create role
Trusted entity, Select: AWS service
For the use case, select: EC2
Trust relationship created
Role name: MediVault-EC2-S3-Role
Description: IAM role allowing the MediVault EC2 instance to access the MediVault S3 scan image bucket.

Create IAM inline Policy (For S3 Access)

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "ListMediVaultBucket",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::medivault-scan-images-bucket01"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "ManageScanImages",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::medivault-scan-images-bucket01/scans/*"
    }
  ]
}
Policy Name: MediVault-Scan-Images-Access

Bucket-level:
s3:ListBucket
Object-level:
s3:GetObject
s3:PutObject

Step - 2: Attach the role to EC2
EC2 → Instances
Select: MediVault-Application
Choose: Actions → Security → Modify IAM role, MediVault-EC2-S3-Role
